    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "After the 1895 fire nearly leveled the area, streets like Market Street were rebuilt and renamed Opelousas Avenue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algiers_Point"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The LeBeuf Plantation House, built in 1840 in French Creole style, now stands as a private residence overlooking the river.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://hnoc.org/publishing/first-draft/walk-along-levee-and-catch-view-overlooked-history-algiers-point"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Along the levee, the Algiers Historical Society has installed a plaque scavenger hunt, each marker sharing a tiny piece of history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
